{"Ali! Welcome to Calgary, brother! I'm stuck at work, so take the Airport Express bus downtown and I'll meet you there.": 12, "There you are! This is downtown. Tomorrow we start your to-do list: newcomer centre, driver's licence, car and insurance. Calgary is going to be good to you.": 18, "First stop: the Centre for Newcomers on 36 Street NE. They helped me with everything when I arrived. Take the CTrain to Rundle, drive, or walk!": 19, "In Alberta, driver's licences are done at a registry agent. McKnight Registry is on Aviation Road NE. Let's go!": 29, "You passed the knowledge test! Your road test is booked: it starts right here. The examiner will ride with you. Obey the speed limits and drive carefully!": 40, "Good morning. Get in the car when you're ready (press F or 🚗). Drive through each checkpoint, keep to the speed limit and don't hit anything. Three mistakes and the test is over.": 42, "Licence done! Before you drive your own car you need insurance. Let's get quotes at TD Auto Insurance Centre on 1 Street SE.": 54, "Your new place is in Martindale. The Genesis Centre in Saddletowne has a gym, a library, a YMCA and community programs. Let's check it out.": 66, "See? You're not alone here. Now let's ride the CTrain so you know how to get downtown.": 71, "Natalia! New semester at Nelson Mandela High! Walk with me, it's just south of the station.": 80, "Natalia, look over there! Those older kids are pushing a Grade 7 kid around and taking his stuff.": 85, "Wait, Natalia! Fighting back or insulting them makes it worse. Watch: stay calm, stand next to him and speak up.": 103, "Hey. Stop. This isn't funny, and you know it.": 104, "Relax. We're just joking around.": 105, "A joke is when everyone is laughing. He isn't laughing.": 106, "Pushing someone and taking his stuff is bullying. And everyone watching knows it.": 107, "So what are you going to do about it?": 108, "I'm walking him to the office, and we're telling a teacher. You can come and explain, or you can leave him alone. Your choice.": 109, "Whatever. Let's go.": 110, "You okay? You didn't do anything wrong. Come on, let's go together.": 111, "Th-thanks. They do this every day. I didn't know what to do.": 113, "See the new girl by herself? That's Amira. She eats lunch alone every day, and that group keeps whispering about her.": 119, "Hi! I'm Natalia, and this is Maya. Do you want to eat lunch with us?": 130, "Really? I just moved here from Syria. My English isn't very good yet.": 131, "Your English is great. And you speak two languages. That's one more than me!": 132, "I heard what you were saying about her clothes.": 133, "Leaving someone out on purpose, or making fun of where they're from or what they wear, is bullying too.": 134, "We didn't mean anything by it.": 135, "Everyone here was new once. Let's make her first week a good one. Come and sit with us.": 136, "Okay... you're right. Sorry.": 137, "Hi Amira. Want to sit with us?": 138, "Thank you. This is the best day since I came to Calgary.": 139, "Natalia, did you see the class group chat? Someone posted an edited photo of Jordan, and everyone's laughing at it.": 144, "Hey. About that photo of Jordan in the group chat.": 160, "It was just a joke. Everyone was posting.": 161, "Everyone posting is exactly why it hurts. One click, and the whole school saw it.": 162, "Online bullying is still bullying. In Alberta, students have to report bullying, even when it happens online.": 163, "I told our teacher, and the post is being taken down. Can you delete what you shared?": 164, "Yeah... you're right. I'm deleting it now.": 165, "Jordan, I'm sorry that happened. You didn't deserve it. We've got your back.": 166, "Thanks, Natalia. I thought nobody cared.": 167, "The principal wants us to visit the younger kids around the school and share what we know about bullying. Three groups are waiting!": 173, "Natalia! The principal asked you to speak at the anti-bullying assembly. Everyone is outside waiting for you!": 189, "Students, please welcome Natalia from Grade 10.": 201, "Hi everyone. This term I saw a Grade 7 kid pushed around, a new student eating lunch alone, and a photo that went around our group chat.": 202, "Every time, lots of people saw it. And most of us did nothing. I used to be one of them.": 203, "Here's what I learned. Bullies need an audience. When we stop laughing and stand next to the person instead, it usually stops.": 204, "You don't have to fight. Stay calm, say \"Stop,\" get the person to safety, and tell an adult.": 205, "If it happens online: don't reply, save the proof, block, report, and tell someone.": 206, "And if you're the one being bullied: it's not your fault. You can call Kids Help Phone any time, day or night.": 207, "Let's make this a school where nobody walks alone. Who's with me?": 208, "We're with you!": 210, "Me too!": 211, "Thank you, Natalia. That took real courage.": 212, "Dad, you've been home alone too much since you retired. The Kerby Centre is right on 7 Avenue. Will you go and see what they offer? For me?": 217, "Tai chi on Tuesdays? I'm signing you up!": 222, "You don't need to drive downtown anymore. Seniors can get a yearly transit pass. Let's walk to the 7 Avenue CTrain platform and ride to City Hall.": 223, "Your doctor said walk every day. Prince's Island Park is flat and beautiful. Let's go!": 232, "\"Hello grandpa, it's me! I'm in jail and I need $2,000 in gift cards right now. Don't tell mom!\"": 242, "New order! Pick up from a local restaurant near you and drive it to the customer. Grab the family car outside or go on foot!": 255, "Jean! Collection day tomorrow. Can you help me sort my stuff? My son put everything in the wrong cart again.": 262, "It snowed last night! Mrs. Kaur next door is 80 and can't shovel. Can you clear her walk and yours?": 276, "Tonight there's a concert at the Saddledome! Park downtown or take the CTrain to Victoria Park / Stampede Station.": 282, "Listen to that crowd! 🎤": 287, "Welcome to Calgary, Leo! I'm Sofia, your guide for the next few days. Let's start with the best view in town: the Calgary Tower, just down 9 Avenue.": 291, "Tip: come back at sunset. You get the city lights and the mountains at the same time.": 301, "Now let's walk Stephen Avenue, one block north. It's a pedestrian street full of restaurants, shops and old sandstone buildings.": 302, "Next, let's catch the CTrain on 7 Avenue. Meet me at City Hall station.": 306, "Calgary is a city of rivers and pathways. Walk west along the Bow River to the Peace Bridge, the red bridge you can see from here.": 315, "East Village is just past City Hall. First stop: the Central Library. Even if you're only visiting, it's worth seeing.": 327, "Now east to where Calgary began: Fort Calgary, where the Bow and Elbow rivers meet.": 332, "Last stop today: Stampede Park, home of the Calgary Stampede.": 337, "You've seen downtown. Before you go further, let's make sure you can explore safely on your own.": 341, "That's my tour, Leo. The rest of the city is yours. Enjoy Calgary!": 358, "Welcome to Calgary, Leo! I'm Sofia, your guide. You picked the best ten days of the year: the Calgary Stampede is on!": 1291, "This is for you. Since about 1950, Calgary has welcomed its visitors with a white cowboy hat. Now you're an honorary Calgarian!": 1293, "Let's go to Stampede Park. The easiest way is the CTrain: the Red Line stops right beside the park, at Victoria Park/Stampede station. Meet me at the big entrance arch.": 1294, "Smell those mini donuts? Let's walk the midway to the Sky Wheel.": 1299, "The Grandstand Show starts soon, on the track south of here. Let's find a spot in the crowd!": 1309, "Every night, the Grandstand Show ends with fireworks over Stampede Park.": 1312, "Yahoo! This is amazing!": 1313, "Get some rest, Leo. Tomorrow I'll show you the city from the Calgary Tower.": 1321, "Good morning, Leo! Today let's start with the best view in town: the Calgary Tower, just down 9 Avenue.": 1322}